+## `jj git ref fetch`
+
+Fetch raw refs or full commit IDs from a Git remote
+
+Each source can be a fully qualified remote ref such as GitHub's `refs/pull/123/head`, or a full Git commit ID.
+
+**Usage:** `jj git ref fetch [OPTIONS] <REF>...`
+
+###### **Arguments:**
+
+* `<REF>` — The remote refs or full Git commit IDs to fetch
+
+###### **Options:**
+
+* `--remote <REMOTE>` — The remote to fetch from (only named remotes are supported)
+
+   By default, this uses the `git.fetch` setting when it matches exactly one remote. If that is not configured, the only remote or the remote named "origin" is used.
